    {
      "name": "offers_to_receive",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/offers_to_receive",
      "annotations": [
        {
          "tag": "domain_includes",
          "value": "gist:Offer",
          "@type": "Annotation"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Relates an offer to the thing expected in return for the offered item.",
      "title": "offers to receive",
      "comments": [
        "This will most often be an amount of money, but could be anything of value, as in swaps."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A vendor makes an offer to receive a particular amount of money in exchange for the offered product; an offer to receive a home in exchange for an amount of money.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/offersToReceive"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/offersToReceive",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "range": "Any",
      "multivalued": true,
      "inlined": true,
      "inlined_as_list": true,
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "owns",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/owns",
      "description": "Relates a party to something that it possesses and controls.",
      "title": "owns",
      "notes": [
        "OWL domain: (gist:Organization | gist:Person)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "The ultimate form of ownership is the right to destroy.",
        "There is a long list of potential range classes."
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/owns"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/owns",
      "owner": "Person",
      "domain_of": [
        "Organization",
        "Person"
      ],
      "range": "Any",
      "multivalued": true,
      "inlined": true,
      "inlined_as_list": true,
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "precedes",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/precedes",
      "description": "A generic ordering relation indicating that the subject comes before the object.",
      "title": "precedes",
      "comments": [
        "The less-than symbol is often used to represent this relation.",
        "This is the transitive version of gist:precedesDirectly.",
        "Typically this predicate would be used asymmetrically and irreflexively, but the ontology does not formalize this."
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/precedes"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/precedes",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "transitive": true,
      "range": "Any",
      "multivalued": true,
      "inlined": true,
      "inlined_as_list": true,
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "precedes_directly",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/precedes_directly",
      "description": "A generic ordering relation indicating that the subject comes immediately before the object.",
      "title": "precedes directly",
      "comments": [
        "If two items in an ordered collection share the same position, they both directly precede the following element.",
        "It is safest to use this property only when the directness has a semantic correspondence with the world. Only break a direct link by inserting an intermediate item when that change corresponds to a change in the world.",
        "Typically this predicate would be used asymmetrically and irreflexively, but the ontology does not formalize this."
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/precedesDirectly"
      ],
      "is_a": "precedes",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/precedesDirectly",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "range": "Any",
      "multivalued": true,
      "inlined": true,
      "inlined_as_list": true,
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "prevents",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/prevents",
      "annotations": [
        {
          "tag": "owl:deprecated",
          "value": true,
          "@type": "Annotation"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Relates an intention to behavior that it prohibits.",
      "title": "prevents",
      "deprecated": "gist marks this term owl:deprecated.",
      "notes": [
        "See guidance on removing this term in the next major release at https://github.com/semanticarts/gist/issues/1380#issuecomment-3617257248"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A city ordinance prohibits jaywalking.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "deprecated_element_has_exact_replacement": "prohibits",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/prevents"
      ],
      "exact_mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/prohibits"
      ],
      "domain": "Intention",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/prevents",
      "owner": "Intention",
      "domain_of": [
        "Intention"
      ],
      "range": "Behavior",
      "multivalued": true,
      "inlined": true,
      "inlined_as_list": true,
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "prohibits",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/prohibits",
      "description": "Relates an intention to a behavior that it forbids or seeks to prevent.",
      "title": "prohibits",
      "comments": [
        "A behavior can be prohibited without being prevented. For example, a speed limit may prohibit driving faster than a stated speed but does not always succeed in preventing drivers from exceeding that speed."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "A city ordinance prohibits jaywalking.",
          "@type": "Example"
        },
        {
          "value": "Private property laws prohibit someone from entering private land marked with a 'No Trespassing' sign.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/prohibits"
      ],
      "domain": "Intention",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/prohibits",
      "owner": "Intention",
      "domain_of": [
        "Intention"
      ],
      "range": "Behavior",
      "multivalued": true,
      "inlined": true,
      "inlined_as_list": true,
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "provides_order_for",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/provides_order_for",
      "description": "Links a member of an ordered collection to the real-world item it represents in that collection.",
      "title": "provides order for",
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/providesOrderFor"
      ],
      "domain": "OrderedMember",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/providesOrderFor",
      "owner": "OrderedMember",
      "domain_of": [
        "OrderedMember"
      ],
      "range": "Any",
      "inlined": true,
      "inlined_as_list": true,
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "refers_to",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/refers_to",
      "description": "Relates something to another resource that it points to, indicates, or references.",
      "title": "refers to",
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/refersTo"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/refersTo",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "range": "Any",
      "multivalued": true,
      "inlined": true,
      "inlined_as_list": true,
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "requires",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/requires",
      "description": "The subject needs the object or makes it necessary, mandatory, or compulsory.",
      "title": "requires",
      "comments": [
        "This predicate is defined generally enough to encompass a few different meanings of the English word 'requires':\n\n  1. To need something or to make something necessary.\n  2. To order or demand something, or to order someone to do something, especially because of a rule or law.\n  3. To make it officially necessary for someone to do something.\n\nImplementations requiring a more specific meaning should define subproperties."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "Humans require air; solar power requires sunshine.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/requires"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/requires",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "range": "Any",
      "multivalued": true,
      "inlined": true,
      "inlined_as_list": true,
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "actual_end_date",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/actual_end_date",
      "description": "The actual date that something ended, with precision of one day.",
      "title": "actual end date",
      "comments": [
        "Used for things where the precision of a date is sufficient, such as most projects, tasks, and the like. Recommended usage is to zero out the hours through microseconds to avoid spurious precision."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "'2021-06-01T00:00:00-06:00'^^xsd:dateTime",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/actualEndDate"
      ],
      "is_a": "actual_end_date_time",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/actualEndDate",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "actual_end_date_time",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/actual_end_date_time",
      "description": "The actual date and time that something ended, with no implied precision.",
      "title": "actual end date time",
      "comments": [
        "This is an abstraction over the various precisions of actual end time, and is not expected to be asserted directly. Values of predicates with different precisions can be compared since they are all formally xsd:datetimes."
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/actualEndDateTime"
      ],
      "is_a": "end_date_time",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/actualEndDateTime",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "actual_end_microsecond",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/actual_end_microsecond",
      "description": "The actual time that something ended, expressed as a system time used for timestamps.",
      "title": "actual end microsecond",
      "comments": [
        "A system time will be as precise as the system can supply, typically at least milliseconds, sometimes microseconds. The convention for timestamps, such as recording a transaction, is to specify just the end point; the start time is rarely needed."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "'2021-06-01T08:03:27.12324-6:00'^^xsd:dateTime",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/actualEndMicrosecond"
      ],
      "is_a": "actual_end_date_time",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/actualEndMicrosecond",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "actual_end_minute",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/actual_end_minute",
      "description": "The actual date and time that something ended, with precision of one minute.",
      "title": "actual end minute",
      "comments": [
        "Used for things like meetings and time card entries, where the hour and minute are important. Recommended usage is to zero out the seconds and microseconds to avoid spurious precision."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "'2021-06-01T08:32:00-06:00'^^xsd:dateTime",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/actualEndMinute"
      ],
      "is_a": "actual_end_date_time",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/actualEndMinute",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "actual_end_year",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/actual_end_year",
      "description": "The actual date that something ended, with precision of one year.",
      "title": "actual end year",
      "comments": [
        "Used for things where the precision of a year is sufficient. Recommended usage is to zero out the hours through microseconds to avoid spurious precision. Note that it is not valid to zero out months and days, so arbitrary values must be included."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "'2021-01-01T00:00:00-06:00'^^xsd:dateTime",
          "@type": "Example"
        },
        {
          "value": "The tenure of the previous chairman of the board ended in 2021.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/actualEndYear"
      ],
      "is_a": "actual_end_date_time",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/actualEndYear",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "actual_start_date",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/actual_start_date",
      "description": "The actual date that something started, with precision of one day.",
      "title": "actual start date",
      "comments": [
        "Used for things where the precision of a date is sufficient, such as most projects, tasks, and the like. Recommended usage is to zero out the hours through microseconds to avoid spurious precision."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "'2021-06-01T00:00:00-06:00'^^xsd:dateTime",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/actualStartDate"
      ],
      "is_a": "actual_start_date_time",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/actualStartDate",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "actual_start_date_time",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/actual_start_date_time",
      "description": "The actual date and time that something started, with no implied precision.",
      "title": "actual start date time",
      "comments": [
        "This is an abstraction over the various precisions of actual start time, and is not expected to be asserted directly. Values of predicates with different precisions can be compared since they are all formally xsd:datetimes."
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/actualStartDateTime"
      ],
      "is_a": "start_date_time",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/actualStartDateTime",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "actual_start_microsecond",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/actual_start_microsecond",
      "description": "The actual time that something started, expressed as a system time used for timestamps.",
      "title": "actual start microsecond",
      "comments": [
        "A system time will be as precise as the system can supply, typically at least milliseconds, sometimes microseconds. The convention for timestamps, such as recording a transaction, is to specify just the end point; the start time is rarely needed. This property is defined for the cases when you do need to capture the runtime of a system process, and is then used in conjunction with gist:actualEndMicrosecond."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "'2021-06-01T08:03:27.12324-6:00'^^xsd:dateTime",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/actualStartMicrosecond"
      ],
      "is_a": "actual_start_date_time",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/actualStartMicrosecond",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "actual_start_minute",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/actual_start_minute",
      "description": "The actual date and time that something started, with precision of one minute.",
      "title": "actual start minute",
      "comments": [
        "Used for things like meetings and time card entries, where the hour and minute are important. Recommended usage is to zero out the seconds and microseconds to avoid spurious precision."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "'2021-06-01T08:32:00-06:00'^^xsd:dateTime",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/actualStartMinute"
      ],
      "is_a": "actual_start_date_time",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/actualStartMinute",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "actual_start_year",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/actual_start_year",
      "description": "The actual date that something started, with precision of one year.",
      "title": "actual start year",
      "comments": [
        "Used for things where the precision of a year is sufficient. Recommended usage is to zero out the hours through microseconds to avoid spurious precision. Note that it is not valid to zero out months and days, so arbitrary values must be included."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "'2021-01-01T00:00:00-06:00'^^xsd:dateTime",
          "@type": "Example"
        },
        {
          "value": "The tenure of the current chairman of the board began in 2021.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/actualStartYear"
      ],
      "is_a": "actual_start_date_time",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/actualStartYear",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "at_date_time",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/at_date_time",
      "description": "The date and time at which something did or will occur, with variants for precision, start and end, and actual vs. planned.",
      "title": "at date time",
      "comments": [
        "This is the top level property for asserting time, and is not expected to be asserted directly.\n\nThe subproperties allow the ontologist to do three things:\n1) Distinguish start and end times.\n2) Indicate whether a time is planned or actual. This is useful for everything from project management to calendar appointments and the like. It is also useful for date effectivities; i.e., something valid up to a planned date).\n3) Distinguish varying levels of precision; sort of a simple version of the Allen functions.\n\nAll datetimes are of the same format: '2021-06-01T08:03:27.12324-6:00'^^xsd:dateTime. This is compatible with and a subset of ISO 8601.\n\nTime zone offset, such as -6:00 (of which there are a few dozen) is recognized in the date itself, as shown. The actual time zone standard (of which there are 131) may optionally be attached to the event or other object itself.\n\nThere will be many historical dates that do not have a time zone offset (e.g., Lincoln's birthday, as well as about 75% of all legacy systems), and in that case the offset can be omitted.\n\nThe conventions for precision that are repeated in each property name are as follows:\n  - *DateTime is an abstraction over the various precisions of its subproperties.\n  - *Date refers to a calendar date (e.g., birthdays and invoice dates) and is assumed to have precision of one day. Time zone offset is allowed.\n  - *Minute refers to clock time; e.g., a meeting will start at 9:15 with a timezone offset. Precision is assumed to have precision of one minute.\n  - *Microsecond refers to system time, and it will be as precise as the system can supply; typically at least milliseconds, sometime microseconds."
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/atDateTime"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/atDateTime",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "birth_date",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/birth_date",
      "description": "The date some living thing was or will be born, with precision of one day.",
      "title": "birth date",
      "comments": [
        "This is a subproperty of gist:startDateTime rather than gist:actualStartDate because some living things have yet to be born. This property refers to a calendar date and is assumed to precision of one day (time zone offset is allowed). It is recommended to zero out the hours through microseconds to avoid spurious precision. Implementations requiring a birthdate to the minute can define a subproperty."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "'2021-06-01T00:00:00-06:00'^^xsd:dateTime",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/birthDate"
      ],
      "is_a": "start_date_time",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/birthDate",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "contained_text",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/contained_text",
      "annotations": [
        {
          "tag": "domain_includes",
          "value": "gist:Content, gist:ContentExpression, gist:Tag, gist:Text",
          "@type": "Annotation"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Relates an entity containing textual information to the string constituting that textual information.",
      "title": "contained text",
      "comments": [
        "If there are multiple strings associated with an entity, it is an implementation decision whether to combine them into a single contained text value or to use multiple contained text assertions."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "The string associated with a tag or with text content.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/containedText"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/containedText",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "range": "string",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "conversion_factor",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/conversion_factor",
      "description": "A value that relates a unit of measure to units of the International System of Units.",
      "title": "conversion factor",
      "notes": [
        "OWL range: (xsd:decimal | xsd:double)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "To convert a numeric value from one unit of measure to another, multiply by the conversion factor of the first unit and then divide by the conversion factor of the second unit.\n\nFor example, to convert 27 feet to yards:\n\n  the conversion factor of foot is 0.3048\n  the conversion factor of yard is 0.9144\n\n  so\n\n  27 feet = (27 x 0.3048) / 0.9144 = 9 yards"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "In the equation 1 inch = 0.0254 meters, the value 0.0254 is the conversion factor of inch.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "see_also": [
        "gist:conversionOffset"
      ],
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/conversionFactor"
      ],
      "domain": "UnitOfMeasure",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/conversionFactor",
      "owner": "UnitOfMeasure",
      "domain_of": [
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "range": "string",
      "any_of": [
        {
          "range": "decimal",
          "@type": "AnonymousSlotExpression"
        },
        {
          "range": "double",
          "@type": "AnonymousSlotExpression"
        }
      ],
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "conversion_offset",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/conversion_offset",
      "description": "A value used along with a conversion factor to relate a unit to its corresponding unit in the International System of Units. In the equation below, the conversion offset is 459.669607 and the conversion factor is 5/9.\n\ny degrees Fahrenheit = (y + 459.669607) x 5/9 degrees Kelvin\n\nTo convert from Fahrenheit to Kelvin, first add the offset and then multiply by the conversion factor.\n\nTo convert from Kelvin to Fahrenheit, reverse the steps: first divide by the conversion factor and then subtract the offset.",
      "title": "conversion offset",
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/conversionOffset"
      ],
      "domain": "UnitOfMeasure",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/conversionOffset",
      "owner": "UnitOfMeasure",
      "domain_of": [
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "range": "decimal",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "death_date",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/death_date",
      "description": "The date some living thing died.",
      "title": "death date",
      "comments": [
        "Refers to a calendar date and is assumed to have precision of one day (time zone offset is allowed). Recommended usage is to zero out the hours through microseconds to avoid spurious precision. Implementations requiring a death date to the minute can define a subproperty."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "'2021-06-01T00:00:00-06:00'^^xsd:dateTime",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/deathDate"
      ],
      "is_a": "actual_end_date",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/deathDate",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "description",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/description",
      "description": "A statement about someone or something's attributes or characteristics.",
      "title": "description",
      "comments": [
        "This property is used to describe instance data which is not part of the ontology. A definition and a description have different semantics. Use skos:definition for a statement of the meaning of a thing and gist:description to describe a thing's attributes, characteristics, or features."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "'The Empire State Building is a 102-story Art Deco skyscraper in midtown Manhattan in New York City. It was designed by Shreve, Lamb & Harmon and built from 1930 to 1931.'",
          "@type": "Example"
        },
        {
          "value": "A person does not have a definition, but might be described as being six feet tall with brown hair and blue eyes; an ontology class or taxonomy term has a definition.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/description"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/description",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "range": "string",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "encrypted_text",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/encrypted_text",
      "description": "Encoded text produced from readable data by an algorithm so that it can only be understood or restored with a decryption key.",
      "title": "encrypted text",
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/encryptedText"
      ],
      "is_a": "contained_text",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/encryptedText",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "range": "string",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "end_date_time",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/end_date_time",
      "description": "The date and time that something ends.",
      "title": "end date time",
      "comments": [
        "This property is neutral along two dimensions: precision (e.g., day, second, millisecond) and actual vs. planned. As such, it will generally not be asserted directly except in special cases (e.g., for time intervals).",
        "Values of predicates with different precisions can be compared since they are all formally xsd:datetimes."
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/endDateTime"
      ],
      "is_a": "at_date_time",
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/endDateTime",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "range": "datetime",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "exponent_of_ampere",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/exponent_of_ampere",
      "description": "The exponent of ampere in a product of powers of base units.",
      "title": "exponent of ampere",
      "notes": [
        "OWL domain: (gist:UnitGroup | gist:UnitOfMeasure)"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "In the equation '1 milliampere = 0.001 x ampere'\n\nthe conversionFactor for milliampere is 0.001\nthe exponent of ampere is 1\nall other exponents are zero\n\nEvery member of a unit group containing milliampere must be a multiple of ampere.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfAmpere"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfAmpere",
      "owner": "UnitOfMeasure",
      "domain_of": [
        "UnitGroup",
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "range": "decimal",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "exponent_of_bit",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/exponent_of_bit",
      "description": "The exponent of bit in a product of powers of base units.",
      "title": "exponent of bit",
      "notes": [
        "OWL domain: (gist:UnitGroup | gist:UnitOfMeasure)"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "In the equation '1 megabit per second = 1000000 x bit per second'\n\nthe conversion factor for megabit per second is 1000000\nthe exponent of bit is 1\nthe exponent of second is -1\nall other exponents are zero\n\nEvery member of a unit group containing megabit per second must be a multiple of bit per second.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfBit"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfBit",
      "owner": "UnitOfMeasure",
      "domain_of": [
        "UnitGroup",
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "range": "decimal",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "exponent_of_candela",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/exponent_of_candela",
      "description": "The exponent of candela in a product of powers of base units.",
      "title": "exponent of candela",
      "notes": [
        "OWL domain: (gist:UnitGroup | gist:UnitOfMeasure)"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "In the equation '1 candlepower = 1 x candela'\n\nthe conversion factor for candlepower is 1\nthe exponent of candela is 1\nall other exponents are zero\n\nEvery member of a unit group containing candlepower must be a multiple of candela.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfCandela"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfCandela",
      "owner": "UnitOfMeasure",
      "domain_of": [
        "UnitGroup",
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "range": "decimal",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "exponent_of_kelvin",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/exponent_of_kelvin",
      "description": "The exponent of Kelvin in a product of powers of base units.",
      "title": "exponent of Kelvin",
      "notes": [
        "OWL domain: (gist:UnitGroup | gist:UnitOfMeasure)"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "In the equation 'y degrees Fahrenheit = (y + 459.6669607) x 5/9 degrees Kelvin'\n\nthe conversion offset for degree Fahrenheit is 459.6669607\nthe conversion factor for degree Fahrenheit is 5/9\nthe exponent of Kelvin is 1\nall other exponents are zero\n\nEvery member of a unit group containing degree Fahrenheit will have a similar equation, with different offset or conversion factor (or both).",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfKelvin"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfKelvin",
      "owner": "UnitOfMeasure",
      "domain_of": [
        "UnitGroup",
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "range": "decimal",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "exponent_of_kilogram",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/exponent_of_kilogram",
      "description": "The exponent of kilogram in a product of powers of base units.",
      "title": "exponent of kilogram",
      "notes": [
        "OWL domain: (gist:UnitGroup | gist:UnitOfMeasure)"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "In the equation '1 millimole per gram = 1 x mole per kilogram'\n\nthe conversion factor for millimole per gram is 1\nthe exponent of mole is 1\nthe exponent of kilogram is -1\nall other exponents are zero\n\nEvery member of a unit group containing millimole per gram must be a multiple of mole per kilogram.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfKilogram"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfKilogram",
      "owner": "UnitOfMeasure",
      "domain_of": [
        "UnitGroup",
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "range": "decimal",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "exponent_of_meter",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/exponent_of_meter",
      "description": "The exponent of meter in a product of powers of base units.",
      "title": "exponent of meter",
      "notes": [
        "OWL domain: (gist:UnitGroup | gist:UnitOfMeasure)"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "In the equation '1 microgram per milliliter = 0.001 x kilogram per meterCubed'\n\nthe conversion factor for microgram per milliliter is 0.001\nthe exponent of kilogram is 1\nthe exponent of meter is -3\nall other exponents are zero\n\nEvery member of a unit group containing microgram per milliliter must be a multiple of kilogram per meterCubed.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfMeter"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfMeter",
      "owner": "UnitOfMeasure",
      "domain_of": [
        "UnitGroup",
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "range": "decimal",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "exponent_of_mole",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/exponent_of_mole",
      "description": "The exponent of mole in a product of powers of base units.",
      "title": "exponent of mole",
      "notes": [
        "OWL domain: (gist:UnitGroup | gist:UnitOfMeasure)"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "In the equation '1 katal = 1 x mole per second'\n\nthe conversion factor for katal is 1\nthe exponent of mole is 1\nthe exponent of second is -1\nall other exponents are zero\n\nEvery member of a unit group containing katal must be a multiple of mole per second.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfMole"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfMole",
      "owner": "UnitOfMeasure",
      "domain_of": [
        "UnitGroup",
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "range": "decimal",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "exponent_of_number",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/exponent_of_number",
      "description": "The exponent of number in a product of powers of base units.",
      "title": "exponent of number",
      "notes": [
        "OWL domain: (gist:UnitGroup | gist:UnitOfMeasure)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "Use when the unit of measure involves a count or other number."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "In the equation '1 beat per minute = 0.016667 x number per second'\n\nthe conversion factor for beat per minute is 0.016667\nthe exponent of number is 1\nthe exponent of second is -1\nall other exponents are zero\n\nEvery member of a unit group containing beat per minute must be a multiple of number per second.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfNumber"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfNumber",
      "owner": "UnitOfMeasure",
      "domain_of": [
        "UnitGroup",
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "range": "decimal",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "exponent_of_other",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/exponent_of_other",
      "description": "Indicates whether a unit of measure can be expressed in terms of the standard exponents (as shown in the examples).",
      "title": "exponent of other",
      "notes": [
        "OWL domain: (gist:UnitGroup | gist:UnitOfMeasure)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "Set the value to 0 if the units of measure in the unit group can be expressed using the standard set of exponents (as in the examples).\n\nOtherwise set the value to 1, which typically means the units of measure in the group use a logarithmic scale."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "Decibel, pH, and octave are units of measure that are logarithmic. Their unit groups have exponent of other = 1.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfOther"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfOther",
      "owner": "UnitOfMeasure",
      "domain_of": [
        "UnitGroup",
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "range": "decimal",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "exponent_of_radian",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/exponent_of_radian",
      "description": "The exponent of radian in a product of powers of base units.",
      "title": "exponent of radian",
      "notes": [
        "OWL domain: (gist:UnitGroup | gist:UnitOfMeasure)"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "In the equation '1 revolution = 6.283 x radian'\n\nthe conversion factor for revolution is 6.283\nthe exponent of radian is 1\nall other exponents are zero\n\nEvery member of a unit group containing revolution must be a multiple of radian.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfRadian"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfRadian",
      "owner": "UnitOfMeasure",
      "domain_of": [
        "UnitGroup",
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "range": "decimal",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "exponent_of_second",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/exponent_of_second",
      "description": "The exponent of second in a product of powers of base units.",
      "title": "exponent of second",
      "notes": [
        "OWL domain: (gist:UnitGroup | gist:UnitOfMeasure)"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "In the equation '1 watt-hour = 3600 x kilogram meterSquared per secondSquared'\n\nthe conversion factor for watt-hour is 3600\nthe exponent of kilogram is 1\nthe exponent of meter is 2\nthe exponent of second is -2\nall other exponents are zero\n\nEvery member of a unit group containing watt-hour must be a multiple of kilogram meterSquared per secondSquared.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfSecond"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfSecond",
      "owner": "UnitOfMeasure",
      "domain_of": [
        "UnitGroup",
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "range": "decimal",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "exponent_of_steradian",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/exponent_of_steradian",
      "description": "The exponent of steradian in a product of powers of base units.",
      "title": "exponent of steradian",
      "notes": [
        "OWL domain: (gist:UnitGroup | gist:UnitOfMeasure)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "Steradian is a measure of solid angle."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "In the equation '1 watt per square meter steradian = 1 x kilogram per secondCubed steradian'\n\nthe conversion factor for watt per square meter steradian is 1\nthe exponent of kilogram is 1\nthe exponent of second is -3\nthe exponent of steradian is -1\nall other exponents are zero\n\nEvery member of a unit group containing watt per square meter steradian must a multiple of kilogram per secondCubed steradian.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfSteradian"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfSteradian",
      "owner": "UnitOfMeasure",
      "domain_of": [
        "UnitGroup",
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "range": "decimal",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "exponent_of_us_dollar",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/exponent_of_us_dollar",
      "description": "The exponent of US Dollar in a product of powers of base units.",
      "title": "exponent of US dollar",
      "notes": [
        "OWL domain: (gist:UnitGroup | gist:UnitOfMeasure)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "The factors for converting from one currency to another change constantly."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "In the equation '1 million dollars per week = 1.65344 x dollar per second'\n\nthe conversion factor for million dollars per week is 1.65344\nthe exponent of US Dollar is 1\nthe exponent of second is -1\nall other exponents are zero\n\nEvery member of a unit group containing million dollars per week must be a multiple of dollar per second.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfUSDollar"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/exponentOfUSDollar",
      "owner": "UnitOfMeasure",
      "domain_of": [
        "UnitGroup",
        "UnitOfMeasure"
      ],
      "range": "decimal",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "id_text",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/id_text",
      "description": "A text string that identifies an individual.",
      "title": "id text",
      "comments": [
        "A common use case would be for preexisting internal company identifiers.",
        "Often, there will be just one identifying text string. More would be appropriate if the individual had different identifiers, such as employee number and social security number. A good way to model that would be to have functional subproperties of idText, such as departmentNumber.",
        "This property is an alternative to using the property gist:isIdentifiedBy in conjunction with instances of the class gist:ID."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "The id text for a car is '4Y1SL65848Z411439'; the id text for the HR department of some company is H31415.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/idText"
      ],
      "slot_uri": "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/idText",
      "owner": "GistThing",
      "domain_of": [
        "GistThing"
      ],
      "range": "string",
      "@type": "SlotDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "is_recorded_at",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/is_recorded_at",
      "description": "The date that something was posted (which is not necessarily the date it occurred). It must be after the date of occurrence, but could be before or after the planned date.",
      "title": "is recorded at",
      "comments": [
        "Precision may vary according to context."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "The date and time a customer payment or stock purchase was posted.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
      "mappings": [
        "https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/isRecordedAt"
