    {
      "name": "CountryGovernment",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/CountryGovernment",
      "description": "A government organization which asserts both sovereignty (i.e., it is not governed by some other government organization) and governance over an entity generally recognized as a country.",
      "title": "Country Government",
      "notes": [
        "OWL subClassOf restrictions: =1^isGovernedBy.gist:CountryGeoRegion; \u22640isGovernedBy.gist:GovernmentOrganization",
        "OWL equivalentClass: (gist:GovernmentOrganization & \u2203^isGovernedBy.gist:CountryGeoRegion)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "While a country government may enter into treaties with other country governments, there are no governing relationships among the treaty members."
      ],
