    {
      "name": "GeoRegion",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/GeoRegion",
      "description": "A bounded region (or set of regions) on the surface of the Earth.",
      "title": "Geographic Region",
      "notes": [
        "OWL subClassOf restrictions: (gist:GeoLocation & \u2203hasMagnitude.\u2203hasAspect=_Aspect_area)"
      ],
      "comments": [
        "A geographic region could be non-contiguous; e.g., the region governed by the US federal government is the contiguous area of the lower 48 states plus Alaska, Hawaii, and overseas territories. Child classes in lower ontologies can make this distinction."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "value": "The bounded shape that defines the region occupied by Crater Lake; the bounded area known as the contiguous USA.",
          "@type": "Example"
        }
      ],
      "in_subset": [
        "gist_core"
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/gist/core",
